WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:17.448
"The election will be next week?" Gliss blinked in surprise.

2
00:00:17.448 --> 00:00:20.726
"Laddno can't do that, can he?"

3
00:00:20.727 --> 00:00:23.534
"He did it," Fala said grimly.

4
00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:29.625
"Venna wants this to be over, so she didn't object. Neither did anyone else."

5
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.917
"That makes sense," Darb said.

6
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:37.536
"The longer the campaign goes on, the more time Laddno has to get people all riled up.

7
00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:41.407
So Venna probably wants the election as soon as possible."

8
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:44.697
"I suppose you're right." Fala looked troubled.

9
00:00:44.697 --> 00:00:49.075
"It doesn't give us nearly as much time to stop Morb though."

10
00:00:49.075 --> 00:00:51.172
"Yeah," Zann said.

11
00:00:51.173 --> 00:00:55.309
"Maybe we should try to rescue my parents before we go to the Far Frontier."

12
00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:57.102
"No," Perda said.

13
00:00:57.103 --> 00:01:03.284
"I'm sure Venna won't let anything bad happen to the prisoners, no matter what happens with the election."

14
00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:05.445
"But—" Zann began.

15
00:01:05.445 --> 00:01:08.077
"Think about it," Perda urged him.

16
00:01:08.078 --> 00:01:15.151
"Morb is a much bigger threat to everyone, including your parents, than anything that might happen with this election.

17
00:01:15.151 --> 00:01:17.592
We have to stop him."

18
00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:22.799
Darb nodded. "Besides, Wyssa won't wait for us if we try to rescue them.

19
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.328
For all we know, she already left for the Far Frontier."

20
00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:32.421
"I'll check." Fala hurried over and grabbed the Remote Eye from a shelf.

21
00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:34.472
She put it to her eye.

22
00:01:34.472 --> 00:01:37.589
"Check the palace square," Perda suggested.

23
00:01:37.589 --> 00:01:39.938
"That's where we saw her last."

24
00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:44.786
Fala nodded. "I don't see her there," she reported after a moment.

25
00:01:44.786 --> 00:01:47.789
"I'm checking the streets nearby too."

26
00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.922
Zann was only half listening. He was still thinking about his parents and Boz.

27
00:01:52.922 --> 00:01:57.927
What if the election took place before Zann and the others returned from the Far Frontier?

28
00:01:57.927 --> 00:01:59.796
And what if Laddno won?

29
00:01:59.796 --> 00:02:03.982
Maff had told the kids that Laddno couldn't be trusted.

30
00:02:03.982 --> 00:02:07.378
What would he decide to do with the prisoners?

31
00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:09.831
Suddenly Zann had an idea.

32
00:02:09.832 --> 00:02:13.689
"Can you use that thing to look inside the palace?" he asked Fala.

33
00:02:13.689 --> 00:02:16.774
She lowered the Eye. "Sure," she said.

34
00:02:16.775 --> 00:02:21.948
"I've been checking on Venna whenever she's there, just in case something strange happens."

35
00:02:21.948 --> 00:02:24.605
"What about the dungeon?" Zann asked.

36
00:02:24.605 --> 00:02:28.151
"Oh, I see." Fala scratched her chin.

37
00:02:28.151 --> 00:02:33.965
"I'm not sure about that. There are probably spells protecting it from spies."

38
00:02:33.965 --> 00:02:36.464
"Can we try?" Zann asked.

39
00:02:36.465 --> 00:02:40.458
"I suppose it wouldn't hurt." Fala raised the Eye again.

40
00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:43.059
After a moment she smiled.

41
00:02:43.059 --> 00:02:48.286
"Hey, it does work! I can see everyone. They all look fine."

42
00:02:48.286 --> 00:02:51.193
She gestured to Zann. "Take a look."

43
00:02:51.193 --> 00:02:53.947
Zann eagerly peered into the Eye.

44
00:02:53.947 --> 00:02:58.371
He gasped as he saw his parents, Boz, Teplo, and the others.

45
00:02:58.371 --> 00:03:02.007
They were talking quietly to one another from their cells.

46
00:03:02.008 --> 00:03:08.191
"I can't believe there are no Shield spells on the dungeon," Gliss said, reaching for the Eye.

47
00:03:08.191 --> 00:03:10.073
"Can I check on my uncle?"

48
00:03:10.073 --> 00:03:13.026
"There probably are spells," Perda said.

49
00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:17.074
"But the Remote Eye is a very old form of magic, remember?

50
00:03:17.075 --> 00:03:20.375
Maybe the spells don't protect against stuff like that."

51
00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:23.194
"That's probably the case," Fala agreed.

52
00:03:23.194 --> 00:03:25.711
"Now let's see if we can locate Wyssa."

53
00:03:25.711 --> 00:03:29.007
The kids took turns scanning the city with the Eye.

54
00:03:29.007 --> 00:03:35.322
Meanwhile Fala tried a few other Search spells, but nothing worked.

55
00:03:35.322 --> 00:03:39.241
"Maybe she really did leave without us," Gliss said.

56
00:03:39.241 --> 00:03:43.167
"Now what are we going to do?" Perda exclaimed.

57
00:03:43.168 --> 00:03:46.354
"I know one place we haven't checked," Darb said.

58
00:03:46.354 --> 00:03:50.317
Zann glanced at his friend, who was scratching Zing with one hand.

59
00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:57.018
The sniffer goose was cuddled up against Darb's other side, honking softly as she drifted off to sleep.

60
00:03:57.018 --> 00:03:59.235
"Where?" Fala asked.

61
00:03:59.236 --> 00:04:03.920
"The zoo," Darb replied. "That's where she took us before, remember?"

62
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.191
"Let me check." Fala raised the Remote Eye to her face.

63
00:04:08.199 --> 00:04:10.658
As soon as she looked through it, she gasped.

64
00:04:10.658 --> 00:04:16.795
"There she is—in a dragon pen! But what's she doing?"

65
00:04:16.795 --> 00:04:18.391
Perda grabbed the Eye.

66
00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:25.127
"It looks like she's cleaning up dragon scales," she reported. "That's weird."

67
00:04:25.127 --> 00:04:30.571
"Not if she needs the scales for some kind of travel spell," Fala pointed out.

68
00:04:30.571 --> 00:04:34.657
"We'd better hurry. She could decide to leave at any moment."

69
00:04:34.657 --> 00:04:39.091
"We?" Zann glanced at Fala. "Are you coming with us?"

70
00:04:39.091 --> 00:04:42.728
She shrugged. "I'd love to see the Far Frontier."

71
00:04:42.728 --> 00:04:46.170
"But what about the animals?" Darb asked.

72
00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:51.128
"I thought you might want to stay with them this time," Fala told Darb, smiling.

73
00:04:51.128 --> 00:04:55.600
"No!" Zann blurted out. "We can't leave Darb behind."

74
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.527
"But he's so good with animals," Fala said.

75
00:04:58.527 --> 00:05:01.417
"This is where he can be most helpful."

76
00:05:01.417 --> 00:05:06.988
Gliss shook her head. "He's most helpful with us," she said firmly.

77
00:05:06.988 --> 00:05:09.256
"That's right," Perda agreed.

78
00:05:09.257 --> 00:05:14.384
"I've lost count of how many times Darb has helped us during our travels."

79
00:05:14.384 --> 00:05:20.390
Zann nodded. "He might not have magic, but he has skills the rest of us don't have."

80
00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:25.046
Fala looked surprised, but she raised both hands in a gesture of surrender.

81
00:05:25.046 --> 00:05:27.643
"All right," she said with a smile.

82
00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:32.317
"You've convinced me. Darb can go with you, and I'll stay here.

83
00:05:32.317 --> 00:05:34.789
But be careful, all right?"

84
00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:41.121
"We will," Zann promised, reaching for his friends' hands. "Zap!"

85
00:05:41.122 --> 00:05:45.651
They landed in a little fountain filled with moon minnows and other fish.

86
00:05:45.651 --> 00:05:50.560
"Ugh, what is it with you and water, Zann?" Gliss complained.

87
00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:54.476
She climbed out and used magic to dry herself and Darb.

88
00:05:54.477 --> 00:05:58.308
"Never mind that." Zann jumped out of the fountain and looked around.

89
00:05:58.309 --> 00:06:01.349
"Which dragon pen was Wyssa in when you saw her?"

90
00:06:01.349 --> 00:06:05.465
"It wasn't the big one with the mean dragons," Perda said.

91
00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:09.393
"I think I saw a cloud glider in the background."

92
00:06:09.393 --> 00:06:11.220
"That pen is this way."

93
00:06:11.221 --> 00:06:17.475
Darb led the way along a path and around a large display of animals native to the Magica Mountains.

94
00:06:17.475 --> 00:06:22.227
When they rounded the corner, Wyssa was just letting herself out of the dragon pen.

95
00:06:22.227 --> 00:06:24.719
She frowned when she spotted the kids.

96
00:06:24.719 --> 00:06:28.141
"It's about time you got here," she snapped.

97
00:06:28.141 --> 00:06:34.964
"I hope you're ready, because we're leaving for the Far Frontier right now."
